{"name":"Afterglow","hex":"#f2e3c5","fetched":"2026-10-20","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"afterglow","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The glow seen in the sky after sunset.","The light emitted by an incandescent object while cooling."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/afterglow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Afterglow","blocks":[{"text":"In meteorology, an afterglow is an optical phenomenon, generally referring to a broad arch of whitish or pinkish sunlight in the twilight sky after sunset, consisting of purple light and bright segment. It consists of several atmospheric optical phenomena. The purple light mainly occurs when the Sun is 2–6° below the horizon, during civil twilight, while the bright segment lasts until the end of the nautical twilight. Similarly, a foreglow is a broad arch of whitish or pinkish sunlight in the twilight sky before sunrise, consisting of purple light and bright segment."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Abendd%C3%A4mmerung_mit_Purpurlicht_und_Schattenstrahlen.jpg/330px-Abendd%C3%A4mmerung_mit_Purpurlicht_und_Schattenstrahlen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Afterglow","wikidata":"Q1141780"},{"title":"Afterglow (Ed Sheeran song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Afterglow\" is a song by English singer Ed Sheeran. Released on 21 December 2020, the song marked Sheeran's first single release in more than 18 months. An accompanying music video features a one-take performance by Sheeran with solo acoustic guitar accompaniment."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/71/Ed_Sheeran_-_Afterglow.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Afterglow_(Ed_Sheeran_song)","wikidata":"Q104407747"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Abendd%C3%A4mmerung_mit_Purpurlicht_und_Schattenstrahlen.jpg/500px